    {
      "id": "claim_b26eb8f5e80c449ea3f695074744cee8",
      "statement": "Store resolves its path from LINKKEEP_HOME (default ~/.linkkeep/bookmarks.json), lazily creates the directory and empty [] file, and exposes load/save/add/remove/count/next_id/clear. Every mutating operation is a full load-modify-save cycle with no caching, so concurrent writers (e.g. CLI and API server) can overwrite each other's changes with no locking.",
      "evidence": [
